  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "Let \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c\\) and \\(d\\) be integers with \\(a\\lt2b,\\) \\(b\\lt3c,\\) and \\(c\\lt4d.\\) If \\(d\\lt100,\\) the largest possible value for \\(a\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2367\\)",
    "B": "\\(2375\\)",
    "C": "\\(2391\\)",
    "D": "\\(2399\\)",
    "E": "\\(2400\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A strict inequality between integers leaves a gap of at least \\(1\\). Starting with the bound on \\(d\\) therefore gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nd&\\le99,\\\\\nc&\\le4d-1\\le395,\\\\\nb&\\le3c-1\\le1184,\\\\\na&\\le2b-1\\le2367.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus no allowed value of \\(a\\) exceeds \\(2367\\).\n\nTo show this bound is possible, choose\n\\[\n(a,b,c,d)=(2367,1184,395,99).\n\\]\nThe original conditions become \\(2367<2368\\), \\(1184<1185\\), \\(395<396\\), and \\(99<100\\), all true. Hence the largest possible value is \\(\\boxed{2367}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
